Binary OPENSTEP nib support
===========================

GormOpenStepTypedStream.m is an Objective-C 1.0 compatible typed stream reader
moved from GNUstep GUI into Gorm's Nib plugin.  It keeps its parsed graph in private C structures
declared in GormOpenStepTypedStream.h.  No NIBMAKER parser source is included.
The historical class layouts used by GormOpenStepNibReader.m were researched
with NIBMAKER-FOR-OPENSTEP's format documentation and examples (commit
bcc7c1a09e0be874f1df259e809517a89b765986).  Thank you to u/These_Magician_3789 on Reddit for his work on the original idea.

The reader accepts streamer versions 3 and 4, both typedstream byte orders,
and checks bounds, references, nesting, array counts, and total allocations.
GormOpenStepNibReader.m converts supported historical objects to an in-memory
binary keyed archive for GormNibWrapperLoader.  Unknown classes and
unsupported layouts fail before application objects are instantiated.

The supported class versions and explicit semantic limitations are encoded
in GormOpenStepNibReader.m.  Tests/README.md describes
the regression tests and fixture generation.

The reader is private to this plugin. It is shared by the Gorm application
and gormtool; NSNib runtime loading is not extended. Existing copyright and
LGPL notices are retained, with COPYING.LIB alongside the moved sources.
Gorm-prefixed symbols permit use with older GUI libraries containing the
original reader without Objective-C class or C symbol collisions.
